course: dictionary
lesson: 9262
title: Southeast on the compass
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A compass has four main points: north, south, east and west. Southeast sits halfway between south and east. On a map with north at the top, southeast is down and to the right.
explain: Look at the words around the word to understand it. «The southeast of England» means the part of England in that direction, not the whole country. Ask yourself: what would fit here? A part of a place fits, so the word is pointing to a region.
explain: In «a southeast wind», the word describes the wind. It is a wind that blows from the southeast. You will also see it written as south-east, and «the South East» is the name of a region of England.
fact: Southeast is written SE on a compass or map.
fact: Southeast is at 135 degrees clockwise from north.
fact: «Southeast Asia» is a region that includes countries such as Thailand, Vietnam, Malaysia and Indonesia.
fact: «The reticulated python of Southeast Asia» is one of the longest snakes; the longest reliably measured ones were about 7 metres.
fact: «The small sun bear» lives in the rainforests of Southeast Asia.
exercise: On a compass, which point is halfway between south and east? | Southwest | West | *Southeast | North
exercise: Which of these countries is in Southeast Asia? | Egypt | *Vietnam | Canada | Norway
exercise: A «southeast wind» blows from which direction? | *From the southeast | From the west | From the north | From the centre of the sea
test: On a map with north at the top, which way is southeast? | Up and left | Down and left | Up and right | *Down and right
test: «The southeast of England» means what? | The sea around England | *The part of England in the southeast direction | The northern edge of England | The whole of England
exam: In which phrase does southeast describe a thing? | Walk to the southeast | *A southeast wind | Travel south-east of the city | The southeast of Wales
